Package: corvusregexecma262
Title: 'ECMA-262' ('JavaScript') Regular Expressions
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matthew", "Adams", email = "matthew.adams@endjin.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Endjin Limited", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Regular expressions with the grammar and the answers of 'ECMA-262',
    the 'RegExp' of 'JavaScript': every flag, lookbehind, named groups, modifier
    groups and the Unicode properties, so that a pattern answers in R as it does
    in a browser or 'Node.js'. Test, match, locate, count, replace and split over
    character vectors, raw vectors of 'UTF-8' (which may hold a NUL) and 'UTF-16'
    code units (which may hold lone surrogates, as a 'JavaScript' string can). A
    pattern without a backreference is matched in time proportional to its size
    times the text. The engine is the
    'corvus-regex-ecma262' 'Rust' crate.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/corvus-dotnet/corvus-regex-ecma262-r
BugReports: https://github.com/corvus-dotnet/corvus-regex-ecma262-r/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc (>= 1.89)
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: yes
